# oracle: pair_style comb + fix qeq/comb - monoclinic HfO2 (LAMMPS examples/comb in.comb.HfO2: over-coordination correction, cor_flag; qeq every step with precision 0.1 to keep the solve within the test time budget, 2 steps, no file keyword)
# oracle-inputs: w58comb_hfo2.data
# oracle-potentials: ffield.comb
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# precision 0.1 (the example uses 0.003): native needs 85 iterations at the setup solve for 0.003 and 31 for 0.1
# (measured with native LAMMPS, black box); the engine spends about 60 ms per iteration on 1500 atoms, so 0.003
# would exceed the 5 s vitest timeout. Measured engine error: thermo max rel 2.7e-13, atoms max abs 2.0e-13.
units		metal
atom_style	charge
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
read_data	w58comb_hfo2.data
mass		1 178.0
mass		2 16.00
velocity	all create 300.1 2398378
pair_style	comb
pair_coeff	* * ffield.comb Hf O
neighbor	0.5 bin
neigh_modify	every 10 delay 10 check yes
timestep        0.00020
thermo_style	custom step temp etotal pe evdwl ecoul press vol lx ly lz xz
thermo_modify	norm yes format float %.15g
thermo		1
fix		1 all nve
fix		2 all qeq/comb 1 0.1
run		2
